  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 126 PM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nMonday through Saturday:\n\n500 mb cluster analysis suggests that the 500 mb flow will\nremain fairly zonal over the region during most of the week,\nbefore a ridge axis develops over the region by Saturday. This\nsetup will continue to allow high pressure to remain east\nnortheast of the region for the first half of the week, with\nanother high developing in the same area later in the week. This\nshould keep the area dry for the week, which is supported by \nensemble members. \n\nTemperatures are expected to gradually rise through the week, \nwith highs climbing well into the 60s early in the week, and \naround or in the lower 70s later in the week. Winds will be \nlight to modest, which may allow for lake breezes/onshore winds \neach day near the lake. \n\nWood",
